 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Introduction to ChromaDB - 7 Simple Steps\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook is a beginner-friendly introduction to ChromaDB, a lightweight vector database. You'll learn the fundamentals step-by-step.\n",
    "\n",
    "## What You'll Learn\n",
    "1. What is ChromaDB and why it matters\n",
    "2. Install and import libraries\n",
    "3. Create a ChromaDB client\n",
    "4. Create a collection\n",
    "5. Add documents to your collection\n",
    "6. Search for similar documents\n",
    "7. Real-world applications"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## STEP 1: What is ChromaDB?\n",
    "\n",
    "**ChromaDB** is a lightweight vector database that makes it easy to:\n",
    "- Store text as numerical vectors (embeddings)\n",
    "- Search for similar text by meaning, not just keywords\n",
    "- Use semantic search in your applications\n",
    "\n",
    "### Why is this useful?\n",
    "Traditional databases search for exact word matches. Vector databases understand *meaning*.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Example:**\n",
    "- Traditional search: \"cat\" won't find \"feline\"\n",
    "- Vector database: Both \"cat\" and \"feline\" are recognized as similar"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## STEP 2: Install and Import Libraries\n",
    "\n",
    "To use ChromaDB in Python, the first step is to install the library.\n",
    "\n",
    "You can install it using `pip` in your terminal or notebook:\n",
    "```bash\n",
    "python -m pip install chromadb sentence-transformers\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "If you are running this in a Jupyter notebook, you can also use the command below.\n",
    "This only needs to be done once for your environment."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Install ChromaDB and dependencies (run this once in your environment)\n",
    "# If you are using Jupyter Notebook, uncomment the line below:\n",
    "# !python -m pip install -q chromadb sentence-transformers\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"✓ Ready to import ChromaDB!\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Now import the necessary modules. These are the main packages we will use throughout this notebook:"\n",
    "\n",
    "- `chromadb`: the vector database itself\n",
    "- `Settings`: configuration for ChromaDB\n",
    "- `embedding_functions`: helper to generate embeddings from text\n",
    "- `Path`: used to create a folder for persistent data storage"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import chromadb\n",
    "from chromadb.config import Settings\n",
    "from chromadb.utils import embedding_functions\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"✓ ChromaDB version: {chromadb.__version__}\")\n",
    "print(\"✓ All imports successful!\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## STEP 3: Create a ChromaDB Client\n",
    "\n",
    "A **client** is your connection to ChromaDB. We'll set up persistent storage so your data survives between notebook runs."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Create a folder to store your vector database\n",
    "persist_dir = Path(\"./chroma_db\")\n",
    "persist_dir.mkdir(exist_ok=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Initialize the ChromaDB client\n",
    "client = chromadb.Client(Settings(\n",
    "    persist_directory=str(persist_dir),\n",
    "    anonymized_telemetry=False,\n",
    "))\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"✓ ChromaDB client created!\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Storage location: {persist_dir.resolve()}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## STEP 4: Create a Collection\n",
    "\n",
    "A **collection** is a container for your documents. Think of it like a table in a traditional database.\n",
    "\n",
    "Each collection needs:\n",
    "- A **name** to identify it\n",
    "- An **embedding function** to convert text into vectors\n",
    "- Optional **metadata** for configuration"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Set up the embedding function (converts text to vectors)\n",
    "embedding_fn = embedding_functions.DefaultEmbeddingFunction()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Create a collection\n",
    "collection = client.get_or_create_collection(\n",
    "    name=\"my_first_collection\",\n",
    "    metadata={\"hnsw:space\": \"cosine\"},\n",
    "    embedding_function=embedding_fn,\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"✓ Collection created: '{collection.name}'\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Documents in collection: {collection.count()}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## STEP 5: Add Documents to Your Collection\n",
    "\n",
    "Add some sample documents. Each document gets:\n",
    "- **Text content**\n",
    "- **A unique ID**\n",
    "- **Metadata** (optional labels)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Sample documents\n",
    "documents = [\n",
    "    \"Machine learning models learn patterns from data.\",\n",
    "    \"Cats are independent and curious animals.\",\n",
    "    \"Vector databases store embeddings for semantic search.\",\n",
    "    \"Neural networks process information like human brains.\",\n",
    "    \"Embeddings represent text as numbers in high dimensions.\",\n",
    "    \"Artificial intelligence is transforming technology.\",\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "# Create unique IDs for each document\n",
    "ids = [f\"doc_{i}\" for i in range(len(documents))]\n",
    "\n",
    "# Add documents to the collection\n",
    "collection.add(\n",
    "    documents=documents,\n",
    "    ids=ids,\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"✓ Documents added successfully!\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Total documents: {collection.count()}\")\n",
    "print(f\"\\nDocuments in collection:\")\n",
    "for i, doc in enumerate(documents):\n",
    "    print(f\"  {i+1}. {doc}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## STEP 6: Search for Similar Documents\n",
    "\n",
    "This is the power of vector databases! Search by **meaning**, not just keywords.\n",
    "\n",
    "The query gets converted to a vector, and ChromaDB finds the most similar documents."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Define a search query\n",
    "query = \"Tell me about machine learning and AI\"\n",
    "\n",
    "# Search for similar documents\n",
    "results = collection.query(\n",
    "    query_texts=[query],\n",
    "    n_results=3,  # Return top 3 matches\n",
    "    include=[\"documents\", \"distances\"],\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Query: '{query}'\")\n",
    "print(f\"\\n🔍 TOP 3 MOST SIMILAR DOCUMENTS:\\n\")\n",
    "\n",
    "for i, (doc, distance) in enumerate(zip(results[\"documents\"][0], results[\"distances\"][0])):\n",
    "    similarity = 1 - distance  # Convert distance to similarity score (0-1)\n",
    "    print(f\"{i+1}. {doc}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"   Distance: {distance:.4f} | Similarity: {similarity:.4f}\")\n",
    "    print()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## STEP 7: Real-World Applications\n",
    "\n",
    "ChromaDB and vector databases power many modern AI applications:\n",
    "\n",
    "### 🔍 **Semantic Search**\n",
    "Find documents by meaning, not just keywords.\n",
    "- Example: Search for \"fast dog\" and find \"quick fox\"\n",
    "\n",
    "### 🤖 **RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation)**\n",
    "Combine an LLM with a vector database to answer questions using your own data.\n",
    "- Example: Ask a chatbot questions about company documentation\n",
    "\n",
    "### 💡 **Recommendation Systems**\n",
    "Find similar products, articles, or users.\n",
    "- Example: Recommend movies similar to ones you've watched\n",
    "\n",
    "### 🔎 **Duplicate Detection**\n",
    "Find near-duplicate records even when they're worded differently.\n",
    "- Example: Identify similar customer complaints\n",
    "\n",
    "### 📊 **Clustering and Analysis**\n",
    "Group similar documents together.\n",
    "- Example: Categorize customer feedback by topic"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Key Takeaways\n",
    "\n",
    "✅ **ChromaDB basics in 7 steps:**\n",
    "1. Understand what ChromaDB is (semantic search database)\n",
    "2. Install and import libraries\n",
    "3. Create a client connection\n",
    "4. Create a collection (container for documents)\n",
    "5. Add documents with embeddings\n",
    "6. Search for semantically similar results\n",
    "7. Apply to real-world problems\n",
    "\n",
    "### Next Steps\n",
    "- Experiment with different queries\n",
    "- Add more documents\n",
    "- Try different embedding models\n",
    "- Build a simple RAG application"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Final summary\n",
    "print(\"\\n\" + \"=\"*50)\n",
    "print(\"CHROMADB INTRODUCTION COMPLETE!\")\n",
    "print(\"=\"*50)\n",
    "print(f\"Collection: {collection.name}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Total documents: {collection.count()}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Location: {persist_dir.resolve()}\")\n",
    "print(\"\\n✓ You now understand ChromaDB basics!\")\n",
    "print(\"✓ Ready to build semantic search applications!\")"
   ]
  }
 ],
